{"metadata":{"extendedModule":"IvorTuning","externalID":"s:10IvorTuning0B6SystemPA2A15WellTemperamentVRszrlE12kirnbergerIIAEvpZ::SYNTHESIZED::s:10IvorTuning15WellTemperamentV","conformance":{"constraints":[{"code":"Self","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is ","type":"text"},{"code":"WellTemperament","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"conformancePrefix":[{"type":"text","text":"Conforms when"}],"availabilityPrefix":[{"type":"text","text":"Available when"}]},"roleHeading":"Type Property","symbolKind":"property","fragments":[{"text":"static","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"identifier","text":"kirnbergerII"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"WellTemperament","preciseIdentifier":"s:10IvorTuning15WellTemperamentV","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"title":"kirnbergerII","role":"symbol","modules":[{"name":"IvorTuning"}]},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"sections":[],"abstract":[{"text":"Kirnberger II (Johann Philipp Kirnberger, c. 1771).","type":"text"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/ivortuning\/welltemperament\/kirnbergerii"]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning","doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning\/WellTemperament"]]},"kind":"symbol","primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"static","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"kirnbergerII","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning\/WellTemperament","text":"WellTemperament","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:10IvorTuning15WellTemperamentV"},{"text":" { ","kind":"text"},{"text":"get","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" }","kind":"text"}],"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"discussion","text":"Discussion","type":"heading","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Two fifths — D→A and A→E — are each narrowed by ½ of the syntonic comma, equal to","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"√(20\/9) ≈ 691.202 cents. One fifth — F♯→C♯ — is narrowed by one schisma","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(32805:32768), equal to 16384:10935 ≈ 699.977 cents. The remaining nine fifths are","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"pure (3:2). The circle closes exactly because one syntonic comma times one schisma","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"equals one Pythagorean comma.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The two half-comma fifths are unusually flat, giving C-adjacent keys very pure"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"thirds while keys with many sharps or flats suffer greatly."}]}]}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning\/WellTemperament\/kirnbergerII"},"references":{"doc://IvorTuning/documentation/IvorTuning/WellTemperament":{"abstract":[{"text":"A tuning system in which all twelve keys are usable but have distinct tonal characters,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"achieved by distributing the Pythagorean comma unevenly around the circle of fifths.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"WellTemperament"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivortuning\/welltemperament","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"WellTemperament"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning\/WellTemperament","title":"WellTemperament","type":"topic"},"doc://IvorTuning/documentation/IvorTuning":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"Musical pitch, interval, and tuning system types.","type":"text"}],"title":"IvorTuning","kind":"symbol","role":"collection","url":"\/documentat